# Railway-Only Backend (mirrors blueprint)

**Canonical:** `blueprint/agent/build-protocol.md` § Railway-only backend

# Railway-Only Backend (No Local Medusa for Clients)

All client surfaces talk to **Railway Medusa** only:

- URL: `config/railway-client.json` → `medusaBase`
- Helpers: `@shc/utils` → `resolveRailwayMedusaBase()`, `resolveRailwayPublishableKey()`
- Localhost / `127.0.0.1` URLs **throw** — never add `localhost:9000` fallbacks

## On every clone / install

`pnpm install` runs `postinstall` → `pnpm env:sync` → writes Railway URLs to:
- `apps/mobile-customer/.env.local`
- `apps/mobile-cook/.env.local`
- `apps/web/.env.local`

## Dev workflow (emulator, simulator, PWA)

```bash
bash scripts/start-mobile-dev.sh   # Metro :8081 + :8082 → Railway API
pnpm web:dev                       # :3001 → Railway API
```

Same backend as TestFlight/APK/Railway PWA — only the JS bundle packaging differs.

## Localhost split (read this — prevents redbox + wrong Docker starts)

| Local service | Port | Required for client dev? | Notes |
|---------------|------|--------------------------|-------|
| **Metro** (JS bundler) | `:8081` customer, `:8082` cook | **Yes** — sim/emulator loads JS from here | `127.0.0.1:8081` in redbox = Metro down, **not** a Railway problem |
| **Medusa API** | `:9000` | **No** — clients use Railway | Never start `docker:up` / `medusa:dev` unless user **explicitly** asks for backend/server work |
| **Medusa Admin UI** | Railway `/app` | Open URL — no local stack | `https://medusa-production-d2ba.up.railway.app/app` · `admin@shc.local` / `supersecret` |

**Railway-only = API/data backend.** Metro on localhost is still normal and required for Expo dev builds.

## Agent playbook: “start iOS simulator / emulator”

**Never** `docker:up`, `medusa:dev`, `medusa:dev:admin`, or `open -a Docker` for simulator/emulator requests.

**One command (Mac iOS):**

```bash
pnpm ios:dev   # Metro :8081+:8082 (daemon) → boot sim → launch customer + cook → verify bundles
```

Equivalent: `bash scripts/start-mobile-dev.sh` (also configures adb reverse when Android emulator is up).

Stale/broken Metro (status OK but redbox / 500 bundle): `METRO_CLEAR=1 pnpm ios:dev`

Per-app reload after UI edits: `pnpm customer:reload` · `pnpm cook:reload`

Scripts detect **stale Metro** (dead pnpm paths after `pnpm install`) and auto-restart when bundle &lt; 5MB or HTTP 500.

## Agent playbook: “medusa admin” / “ops dashboard”

Open **Railway Admin** in browser — no local Postgres/Docker:

`https://medusa-production-d2ba.up.railway.app/app` → SHC Ops at `/app/shc-ops`

Local `pnpm medusa:dev:admin` is **backend-track only** when editing `apps/medusa` code — not the default answer.

## Forbidden

- `EXPO_PUBLIC_MEDUSA_BASE=http://localhost:9000`
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SHC_API_BASE=http://localhost:9000`
- Docs/scripts telling users to run `docker:up && medusa:dev` for client testing
- `USE_REAL_MEDUSA` toggles or mock fallbacks in runtime api-clients
- Starting **Docker / local Medusa** when user asks for simulator, emulator, or admin UI (see playbooks above)
- Saying “ready” without verifying Metro `:8081/status` + bundle size when launching mobile sim

## Medusa app code (`apps/medusa`)

Backend source still lives in-repo for Railway deploys. `pnpm medusa:dev` is for **server development only**, not for pointing clients at localhost.